  <notes>Verse block: the lines are set in italic with names in roman capitals (MARTE, PATRIÆ, PRINCEPS, DUX BONE, HEBRÆO, MYSTES). Printed lines are indented in a stepped arrangement; the stanza is kept as one paragraph. The ornament below the signature is a woodcut (a cherub-like head between foliage and scrolls with pendant fringes); it is not text and is not transcribed. "AD" at the bottom right is a catchword. The printed "Jonauit" carries a capital J at the start of the word, as printed; "Vestræ" and "deditissimus" are the closing dedication to the addressee.</notes>
